End-to-end AWS cloud migration case study for a 3-tier payment application, covering on-premises/VMware discovery, dependency assessment, AWS architecture, security, Terraform infrastructure, migration waves, cutover, rollback, and operational readiness. Based on real-world cloud migration experience and sanitized for public sharing.

# Business Scenario

A payment application is currently running in an on-premises VMware environment.

The platform supports 24×7 payment processing and consists of:

Web/application tier
Database tier
Shared file storage
Internal load balancer
Monitoring
Network and security controls

The organization wants to migrate the platform to AWS while:

Minimizing application downtime
Maintaining business continuity
Meeting defined RTO/RPO
Improving scalability
Improving operational visibility
Standardizing infrastructure through Terraform
Migration objectives
Requirement	Target
Migration approach	Phased migration
Downtime	Minimal
RTO	30 minutes
RPO	5 minutes
Availability	Multi-AZ
Infrastructure	AWS
IaC	Terraform
CI/CD	GitLab CI/CD
Monitoring	CloudWatch
Security	IAM, SG, encryption, secrets
Database	PostgreSQL
Application	3-tier

Note: The numbers above are illustrative/sanitized for the public case study.
